WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:15.340
Friends, among all the health threats that
exist in the world today, right now it’s

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:18.590
a virus that stands head and shoulders above
all others.

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:22.000
There is virtually no headline or programme
that doesn't address the news.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.430
It's the news event of the year.

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:27.279
And the truth is, that to this day, it is
not about the number of people infected or

00:00:27.279 --> 00:00:31.800
the apparent lethality that worries us, it
is above all else the newness of the threat

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:37.110
and the fact that we still do not know exactly
what we are facing that makes it so terrifying.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:42.909
There are no vaccines and beyond the treatment
of symptoms, there isn’t a specific cure.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:46.150
I'm sure you don't need any more clues at
this point to know what we're talking about,

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:47.150
do you?

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:51.589
Yes, exactly, we're talking about Wuhan's
famous Coronavirus, the COVID-19 disease that

00:00:51.589 --> 00:00:56.250
is spreading around the world and has not
yet reached its peak of infection.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:01:02.420
At the time of producing this video, the virus
has reached 37 countries, more than 90,000

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:07.240
people have been infected and of them, more
than 3,200 have succumbed to the disease.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:11.890
As you’re probably aware, this new strain
of Coronavirus, the seventh one to be identified,

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:17.110
is believed to have originated in a food market
in the Chinese city of Wuhan, where live animals,

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:22.320
including wild animals, were sold.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.990
As you can imagine, such an epidemic can have
a great impact... on all levels.

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:30.580
And, look, I'm not just talking about health,
but also about the knock-on effects in politics

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:32.870
and, of course, the consequences for the economy.

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:38.590
(AUDIO: China’s Coronavirus Has Revived
Global Economic Fears - The New York Times)

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:44.050
(AUDIO: Alibaba Warns Virus Having Broad Impact
on Chinese Economy - Bloomberg)

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:50.610
(AUDIO: Factories Facing "Severe" Labor Shortages
In China, U.S. Business Group Says - Forbes

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:54.040
“Stocks tumble as haven assets rally on
coronavirus fears

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:55.040
Investors shift away from riskier assets on
signs outbreak is gathering pace outside China

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:59.409
Investors have rushed out of equities and
into havens such as gold and US government

00:01:59.409 --> 00:02:05.030
bonds following a surge in coronavirus cases
in Italy, South Korea and Iran over the weekend

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:08.670
that intensified concerns over the global
impact of the virus.”)

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:13.390
Of course, the epicentre, the full brunt of
this terrible story is being felt in China,

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:18.700
especially in Hubei Province, which is where
Wuhan is located, the city where the outbreak

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:20.489
allegedly started.

00:02:20.489 --> 00:02:26.670
China has suffered intensely from the threat
of the Coronavirus: city streets are now virtually

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:30.849
empty, many factories, malls and shops of
all kinds have closed their doors.

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:33.120
People are afraid to use public transport.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.660
And some places like Hubei Province are still
paralyzed.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:37.540
Locked down in quarantine.

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:40.849
People can't leave their houses and even car
journeys have been banned.

00:02:40.849 --> 00:02:44.489
Written permits are needed for everything,
and you can no longer go to the pharmacy or

00:02:44.489 --> 00:02:49.049
do your grocery shopping, now everything has
to be ordered online.

00:02:49.049 --> 00:02:55.459
Dear friends, in an upcoming video here on
VisualPolitik, we will discuss in detail what

00:02:55.459 --> 00:02:58.739
the long-term economic consequences of such
a threat might be.

00:02:58.739 --> 00:03:03.379
So you know, if you haven't already done so,
don't miss out, subscribe to find out what’s

00:03:03.379 --> 00:03:04.379
going on.

00:03:04.379 --> 00:03:07.260
However, this time we're going to take a 90-degree
turn.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:11.299
In this video, we're talking about Cathay
Pacific, Hong Kong’s flagship airline that's

00:03:11.299 --> 00:03:13.590
having a really hard time right now.

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:18.530
Wait a minute, why on earth are we going to
talk about an airline?

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:23.360
Well, because this company, Cathay Pacific,
is, a good example of how everything related

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:27.569
to economics can suffer with the outbreak
of the Coronavirus and also how not even this

00:03:27.569 --> 00:03:32.799
major healt threat has been enough to stop
the expansionism of the Chinese government.

00:03:32.799 --> 00:03:34.719
But...

00:03:34.719 --> 00:03:35.719
Let's start at the beginning.

00:03:35.719 --> 00:03:39.590
While companies around the world have begun
to suffer due to a scarcity in components

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:44.400
from Chinese suppliers due to factory closures
and a lack of workers, Cathay Pacific is missing

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.400
passengers.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:49.599
Okay, in Hong Kong cases still hover around
100, but fear is in the air.

00:03:49.599 --> 00:03:54.540
And friends, this epidemic couldn’t have
come at a worse time for this airline.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:59.169
Anti-government protests that have been burning
in the streets of Hong Kong for months, and

00:03:59.169 --> 00:04:02.829
of which we have already discussed here on
VisualPolitik, have caused arrivals of visitors

00:04:02.829 --> 00:04:09.819
and tourists to the city to fall faster than
the value of the Argentinian Peso.

00:04:09.819 --> 00:04:12.980
(CHART)

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:17.989
In 2019, 9 million fewer visitors arrived
in Hong Kong compared with the previous year.

00:04:17.989 --> 00:04:19.280
And now with the coronavirus...

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.840
All signs indicate that 2020 could be even
worse.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:24.480
In fact, check this out.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:29.880
During January 2020, visitors to Hong Kong
dropped 53% compared to the same month in

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:30.880
the previous year.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:35.440
And in January 2020, the spectre of this coronavirus
was relatively smaller.

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:39.560
That makes the forecasts for the coming months
pretty bleak.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:45.010
So, what kind of companies do you think suffer
the most in circumstances like this?

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:46.010
Well...

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:47.460
Yes, obviously hotels and airlines.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:51.430
Those kinds of businesses feel the pinch as
people stay home.

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:56.310
Friends, the political crisis in Hong Kong
was a major blow to Cathay Pacific.

00:04:56.310 --> 00:05:00.810
Now the impact of the Coronavirus may be the
last straw.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:04.840
Now, exactly how great is the fallout?

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:08.210
How is the appearance of the Coronavirus affecting
this airline?

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:09.400
What steps are they taking?

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:14.240
What is the future of a company that has already
been suffering an unprecedented crisis for

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:16.280
almost a year?

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:21.050
Over the past few years, Cathay Pacific's
story has been filled with misfortune, political

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:24.790
blackmail, threats and political layoffs.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:29.340
Listen to this.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:33.900
(CATHAY’S ‘ANNUS HORRIBILIS’)

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:39.210
Friends, before we start talking about Cathay
Pacific's problems, I think it's best to get

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:43.650
a deeper understanding of the company.

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:47.430
Cathay Pacific is a flagship company, Hong
Kong's most important company.

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:51.599
And we're not exactly talking about a small
airline, but one of the largest air groups

00:05:51.599 --> 00:05:52.599
across the Asian continent.

00:05:52.599 --> 00:05:58.449
For you to get an idea, the size of its fleet
today is 152 aircraft, all of them wide-body

00:05:58.449 --> 00:06:00.580
craft.

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:06.460
And not only that, besides the main airline
brand, this company also operates another

00:06:06.460 --> 00:06:11.569
passenger subsidiary, Cathay Dragon, with
a fleet of 48 more aircraft, and a cargo subsidiary,

00:06:11.569 --> 00:06:13.229
Air Hong Kong, with 11 aircraft.

00:06:13.229 --> 00:06:18.159
That is, we are talking about an air group
with more than 200 operational aircraft and

00:06:18.159 --> 00:06:21.750
routes to 130 destinations across the globe.

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:28.010
However, 2019 turned out to be a horrible
year.

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:31.169
And as we have mentioned, 2020 could be even
worse.

00:06:31.169 --> 00:06:37.550
During the first month of 2020, passenger
arrivals at Hong Kong airport decreased by

00:06:37.550 --> 00:06:38.580
40% year-on-year.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:43.520
This has meant that both the number of passengers
and the volume of cargo carried by this airline

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:46.530
has been in freefall in recent months.

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:53.540
You see, in aviation, occupancy data is usually
measured by the passenger load coefficient,

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:57.910
which calculates the relationship between
seats per kilometre offered by an airline

00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:03.229
and seats that were occupied.

00:07:03.229 --> 00:07:04.830
(CHART)

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:09.039
As you can see, the second half of 2019 was
horrible for Cathay compared to 2018.

00:07:09.039 --> 00:07:14.240
And it’s a similar story with the cargo
subsidiary.

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:18.719
In other words, this is a clear illustration
of the economic damage that has resulted from

00:07:18.719 --> 00:07:22.190
the difficult political situation that Hong
Kong is going through at present.

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:25.090
It also explains news stories like this one:

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:28.930
(AUDIO: Hong Kong Suffers First Annual Recession
in a Decade.

00:07:28.930 --> 00:07:32.990
Hong Kong’s economy contracted by 1.2% in
2019.

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:37.169
Global trade turbulence and months of anti
government protests pushed the city into its

00:07:37.169 --> 00:07:42.289
first annual recession since the depths of
the global financial crisis in 2009.

00:07:42.289 --> 00:07:43.419
WSJ)

00:07:43.419 --> 00:07:46.400
And now there’s also the coronavirus to
contend with.

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:51.599
(AUDIO: Cathay Pacific issues profit warning
after coronavirus hits service - The Guardian)

00:07:51.599 --> 00:07:55.690
Perhaps all of this explains why Cathay's
shares have reached their lowest price in

00:07:55.690 --> 00:07:58.610
more than 10 years.

00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:03.590
However,, this is not the only threat facing
the airline, nor the population of Hong Kong.

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:07.830
Because the truth is that we may be witnessing
what is perhaps the last move in a game that

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:10.529
could put an end to Hong Kong as we know it.

00:08:10.529 --> 00:08:14.680
Check this out:

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:20.860
(IS THE FUTURE IN CHINA’S HANDS?)

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:26.469
Friends, when a company is struggling, apart
from the shareholders, the first ones to notice

00:08:26.469 --> 00:08:31.819
the consequences are usually employees.

00:08:31.819 --> 00:08:36.450
Following the coronavirus epidemic, Cathay
has been forced to suspend 90% of its flights

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:39.690
to mainland China and 30% of all its flights
globally.

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:43.950
With such severe cuts to their services, the
company has asked 27,000 employees to take

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:48.950
three weeks of unpaid leave to reduce fixed
costs and try to cope with the difficult situation

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:51.550
it is faced with.

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:55.770
However, this is not the only problem facing
this airline.

00:08:55.770 --> 00:08:58.650
Remember how we were talking about the protests
in Hong Kong?

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:02.520
Well, friends, the drop in visitor numbers
was by no means the only negative impact from

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:05.100
that event that Cathay Pacific faced.

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:10.400
Are you familiar with the consequences of
angering the Chinese regime?

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:15.110
Well, let's just say that Cathay completed
an accelerated master's degree in the matter.

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:19.090
You see, after the protests broke out, several
workers who participated in them were unlucky

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:21.940
enough to be identified by the Chinese authorities.

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:26.150
And do you know what Beijing did?

00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:29.840
Well, they said: Good job controlling your
employees; they keep participating in the

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:30.840
protests.

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:34.230
Soon you're going to realise the error of
your ways – soon you won't have a single

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:35.690
permit to fly in China.

00:09:35.690 --> 00:09:41.040
You know, trademark authoritarian moves.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:44.690
The pressure from the Chinese government that
said that the airline had not done enough

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:49.710
to control the political activities of its
workers ended up in the resignation of former

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:54.720
CEO Rupert Hogg and the President of Cathy
himself, John Slosar.

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:58.270
Following these two resignations, the airline
launched a heavy-handed policy against all

00:09:58.270 --> 00:10:02.660
those employees who participated in the protests
and even those who had showed support for

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:04.700
the cause through social media campaigns.

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:08.780
At least two dozen workers were instantly
dismissed.

00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:14.800
Yes, China forcing a company to curb the political
participation of its employees.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:21.120
It’s crazy, but that's just how Xi Jinping's
government rolls.

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:23.530
But this shady story doesn't end there.

00:10:23.530 --> 00:10:27.520
Here on VisualPolitik we have already told
you how the Republic of China is trying, by

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:30.780
all means possible, to consolidate its power
in Hong Kong.

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:35.000
Well... now it seems the Chinese government
has found a new way to attack.

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:38.000
Let me explain.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:41.370
Cathay Pacific's current financial problems
stemming from the Hong Kong protests and exacerbated

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:45.290
by the coronavirus might just be the golden
opportunity for China, once and for all, to

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:48.620
take control of Hong Kong’s main transportation
provider.

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:50.150
And it’s nothing if not determined.

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:55.440
For more than a decade, China's quintessential
state airline, Air China, has owned 30% of

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:56.450
Cathay Pacific's shares.

00:10:56.450 --> 00:11:01.000
It is the second largest shareholder behind
Hong Kong group Swire Pacific, which controls

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:04.660
45% of the shares.

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:08.830
So the truth is that if the Hong Kong airline's
bad run continues, China could be in an optimal

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:11.860
position to inject capital and take control
of the company.

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:16.160
In this way, its control over the lives of
Hong Kongers and the future of this city would

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:18.090
be even greater.

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:24.380
Yes, this shows us that Xi Jinping's government
knows how to take advantage of all situations,

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:28.910
even one as terrible as that fostered by Coronavirus.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:33.850
In any case, when it comes to Hong Kong, it
seems that in Beijing they have a clear idea:

00:11:33.850 --> 00:11:37.040
the worse it gets down there, the better it
will be for China.

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:40.870
Friends, Cathay Pacific is nothing more than
a microcosm of everything that is happening

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:46.020
in Hong Kong, a socially burning city that
every day seems closer to being devoured by

00:11:46.020 --> 00:11:47.230
the Chinese giant.

